.TH "GF-ANNOTATIONS-PATCH-ANNOTATION" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-annotations-patch-annotation - Patches annotation


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf annotations patch-annotation [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Patches annotation

.PP
Updates one or more properties of an annotation that matches the specified ID. This operation currently supports updating of the \fBtext\fR, \fBtags\fR, \fBtime\fR and \fBtimeEnd\fR properties. This is available in Grafana 6.0.0-beta2 and above.

.PP
Body schema (PatchAnnotationsCmd):
{
  "data": any,
  "id": number,
  "tags": [string],
  "text": string,
  "time": number,
  "timeEnd": number
}


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--annotation-id\fP=""
	AnnotationID

.PP
\fB--body\fP=""
	The path to the body json file or json string. For example, --body=/path/to/body.json or --body='{"foo": "bar"}'

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for patch-annotation


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	Organization ID (env: GF_ORG_ID)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgf-annotations(1)\fP
